# TypeScript

- Use strict typing; avoid `any` unless bridging untyped third-party APIs.
- Prefer `type` for unions and object shapes; use `interface` for extendable contracts.
- Export types from `src/types/` when shared across layers.
- Use `unknown` in catch blocks, then narrow before use.

```typescript
// ❌ BAD
catch (e) {
  console.log(e.message);
}

// ✅ GOOD
catch (error) {
  const message = error instanceof Error ? error.message : "Unknown error";
  throw new Error(`Operation failed: ${message}`, { cause: error });
}
```
